    "created_at": "2026-05-05T09:58:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-05-05T09:58:33Z",
    "body": "I don't personally think this should be hacked into \"show the picker\", we should just define a \"close the picker\" algorithm and call it as part of removal steps for input and select elements. Show the picker is already fairly handwaivy so this can be just as handwaivy, the algorithm name alone is pretty clear what is intended. And then like said above `:open` should make this actually testable via WPT now.\n\nI guess there's moveBefore too and what to do there, I think we should leave it open but perhaps we should define some other handwaivy moving steps for input and select to say that any UA provided picker should be repositioned to the new DOM location? - Though that's perhaps a separate issue.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
